---
import {supply,comparePower} from '../power-sensitivity.mjs';
const cases=[['planned-mix','base','Historical RTX/B300 mix — base'],['b200-scale','base','Historical B200 expansion — base'],['b200-scale','favorable','Historical B200 expansion — favorable, uncontracted']].map(([id,kind,label])=>({id,kind,label,...comparePower(id,kind)}));
const usd=(n:number)=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(n);
---
<section id="power-case" class="inv-power-case" aria-labelledby="power-case-title">
  <p class="inv-eyebrow">POWER STRATEGY / OWNER UPDATE</p>
  <h3 id="power-case-title">Solar, storage and gas.<br/>Prove the delivered advantage.</h3>
  <p>Management reports an agreement for behind-the-meter supply using solar, batteries and gas generators, with a cost below 7¢/kWh. The agreement and full cost coverage have not been reviewed. Exclusive continuous capacity and the operating date remain to be confirmed.</p>
  <details class="inv-details"><summary>Historical energy-price sensitivity — earlier platform and cost assumptions</summary>
  <p>The historical cases below predate the complete Supermicro plan, new cooling scope and unresolved BC LLC payment. They are not updated deployment economics. They test a 7¢/kWh energy input, keeping the original reserve, demand charges and every other cost and revenue assumption unchanged. Separate generation, maintenance, fuel and equipment obligations remain to be priced.</p>
  <div class="inv-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Historical power price sensitivity; scroll horizontally on small screens"><table><caption>Historical energy-price sensitivity · 7¢ versus 10¢/kWh · both escalate 3% annually</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Scenario</th><th scope="col">Five-year cash improvement</th><th scope="col">Net cash profit / loss at 7¢</th><th scope="col">NPV at 15%</th></tr></thead><tbody>{cases.map(c=><tr><th scope="row">{c.label}</th><td>{usd(c.netCashImprovement)}</td><td>{usd(c.result.project.netProfit)}</td><td>{usd(c.result.project.npv)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p><strong>What this means:</strong> Lower energy cost helps, but it does not make either base-case owned-GPU deployment profitable. The favorable B200 case still depends on 90% stabilized paid occupancy and five years of flat GPU pricing. Neither those customer terms nor the power cost scope is verified.</p>
  <details class="inv-details"><summary>What establishes an investable power advantage?</summary><ul><li>Documented supply rights, duration, delivery date and exclusive continuous kW after other campus loads.</li><li>Delivered cost including {supply.costItemsToConfirm.slice(0,5).join(', ').toLowerCase()}.</li><li>Engineer-approved power quality, cooling, redundancy and outage operation. Storage capacity in kWh must support the required runtime at the actual load.</li><li>A customer who commits to pay for the resulting service, with clear minimum payments, service credits and cancellation terms.</li></ul><p>Power availability could also affect commissioning speed and customer value. No earlier revenue, reliability premium, electricity resale or ancillary-service income is modeled without evidence.</p></details>
  <div class="inv-actions">{cases.map(c=><button type="button" class="inv-outline" disabled data-underwriting-option={c.id} data-underwriting-case={c.kind} data-underwriting-power="reported">Load {c.label.toLowerCase()} at 7¢</button>)}</div>
  </details>
</section>
<style>
  .inv-power-case{margin:3rem 0;padding:2rem;border:1px solid #547064;border-radius:1rem;background:#143b2d}
  .inv-power-case h3{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:1.15;margin:1rem 0}
  .inv-power-case table{min-width:700px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .inv-power-case caption{text-align:left;padding:1rem 0;color:#c4d9cd}
  .inv-power-case th,.inv-power-case td{text-align:left;padding:.85rem;border-bottom:1px solid #476555;vertical-align:top}
  .inv-power-case li{margin:.8rem 0;line-height:1.6}
  @media(max-width:600px){.inv-power-case{padding:1rem}}
</style>
